<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="impala_max_fragment_instances_per_node">

  <title>MAX_FRAGMENT_INSTANCES_PER_NODE Query Option</title>
  <titlealts audience="PDF"><navtitle>MAX FRAGMENT INSTANCES PER NODE</navtitle></titlealts>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala Query Options"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Performance"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Developers"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Data Analysts"/>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <conbody>
    <p>The <codeph>MAX_FRAGMENT_INSTANCES_PER_NODE</codeph> query option sets the maximum number of
      fragment instances per node that the processing cost algorithm assigns to a query
      fragment.</p>
    <p>The recommended practice is to set this query option to a value lower than or equal to the
      number of physical cores in an executor node. This query option is ignored if the selected
      executor group has a lower <codeph>max-query-cpu-core-per-node-limit</codeph> configuration,
      or if the <codeph>PROCESSING_COST_MIN_THREADS</codeph> query option has a higher value.</p>
    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/type_integer"/>
    <p><b>Allowed values:</b> Integers in the range [1, 128].</p>
    <p><b>Default:</b> 128</p>
    <p><b>Added in:</b><keyword keyref="impala43" id="IMPALA-12091"/></p>
  </conbody>
</concept>
